From: pat <pi3iman@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mediatek/ppe: prefetch next flow entry data in lookup hot path

In __mtk_ppe_check_skb() the per-bucket hlist walk calls
mtk_flow_entry_match() which reads entry->data (a mtk_foe_entry stored
at a separate cache line from the hlist node the walk just dereferenced).
Issue a prefetch of the next entry's ->data one iteration ahead to hide
the cache miss on longer hash chains. mtk_flow_entry objects are cached
slab memory (unlike the uncached coherent foe_table), so they are a
valid prefetch target.

Pure read hint: touches no iowrite32 sequence and no aging/GC logic.
Context matches vanilla 6.12 mtk_ppe.c (4-arg mtk_flow_entry_match with
entry_len), independent of the PPPQ patches above.

Signed-off-by: pat <pi3iman@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/if_ether.h>
 #include <linux/if_vlan.h>
+#include <linux/prefetch.h>
 
 #include <net/dst_metadata.h>
 #include <net/dsa.h>
@@ -814,6 +815,15 @@
 	memcpy(&foe, hwe, entry_len);
 
 	hlist_for_each_entry_safe(entry, n, head, list) {
+		/* mtk_flow_entry_match() below reads entry->data (a separate
+		 * cache line from the list node just followed). Prefetch the
+		 * next entry's flow data while comparing the current one, to
+		 * hide the miss on longer hash chains.
+		 */
+		if (n)
+			prefetch(&hlist_entry(n, struct mtk_flow_entry,
+					      list)->data);
+
 		if (found ||
 		    !mtk_flow_entry_match(ppe->eth, entry, &foe, entry_len)) {
 			if (entry->hash != 0xffff)
